  "text": "Immortalized APOE4 astrocytes expressed more V-ATPase subunit V0D1 protein than APOE3 astrocytes. This is a step that could favour organelle acidification, although measured organelle pH was not lower.",
  "description": "Immortalized astrocytes from human APOE3- and APOE4-targeted-replacement mice, cultured with 10% FBS. Western blot used anti-V0D1 (ab56441), normalized to β-actin. N = 4. Caveat: mouse immortalized astrocytes, not human. V0D1 level is a proxy for pump abundance, not for endosomal pH. Bafilomycin experiments in the paper suggest greater V-ATPase activity, but the authors infer the extra protons are exchanged for Ca2+ via CAX, so pH is not lowered.",
